
DFR.EXE is a fully functional textfile reader.  Entering DFR
without command line parameters gives a reminder of usage, namely:

 The Dolphin File Reader, version 3.2, Copyright 1991 Dolphin Software
 Use "DFR filepath" to read file(s).  Filepath may contain wildcards.
 Add /b to the command line for BIOS video output.

You may browse multiple files by using wildcards in the file specifi-
cation, e.g. DFR *.TXT. If more than one readable textfile is found
then the program will initially display a scrollable list of files at
the bottom right corner of the screen.  Press Enter or Escape to browse
the currently-displayed file, otherwise scroll through the list and
press Enter at the file you wish to read.  If this happens to be a
non-readable file then the next readable file will be displayed instead.

F1 displays a help screen.  Control-L brings up the list of files (if there
is more than one readable file).  Control-S allows you to search the
current file for a character string.  If a match is found then pressing
Control-S again will find the next match (if any).  Searches are not
case-sensitive.  Control-D takes you temporarily to DOS; enter "EXIT" to
return to the program.

The Dolphin File Reader supports 25-, 43- and 50-row modes, and uses
whichever mode is in effect when the program starts.  Files of up to about
350K in size are handled. If you want the program to use BIOS video output,
rather than writing directly to video RAM (which is quicker), use the /b
option.

